## 938

The given domain is [-1,6]. The solid rising source curve runs from (-1,-1)
to (6,3), crossing y=5/2 at (4,5/2).

- f(x)=2.5: {4}.
- f(x)<2.5: [-1,4).
- f(x)>2.5: (4,6].

The source curve is below the queried horizontal level to the left of the
crossing and above it to the right. Strict inequalities exclude 4; the domain
includes both outer endpoints. No analytic formula is assumed.

## 939

The given domain is [-2,5]. The falling source curve crosses y=-1/2 at
(1,-1/2) and crosses the origin.

- g(x)=-0.5: {1}.
- g(x)<-0.5: (1,5].
- g(x)>-0.5: [-2,1).

The left endpoint is (-2,3). At x=5 the source ink is near y=-1 and below
the queried level; its unneeded exact ordinate is not asserted. The strict
inequalities exclude 1; the original domain includes -2 and 5.

## 942

Time is in seconds; speed is in metres/second. Source grid steps are 5 seconds
and 2 metres/second. The trace vertices, in order, are:

(0,0), (15,16), (30,16), (35,8), (45,8), (50,0), (60,0),
(70,16), (90,16), (100,0), (115,0), (120,8), (140,8), (150,0).

- Increasing: [0,15], [60,70], [115,120].
- Decreasing: [30,35], [45,50], [90,100], [140,150].
- Constant: [15,30] at 16; [35,45] at 8; [50,60] at 0;
  [70,90] at 16; [100,115] at 0; [120,140] at 8.

These are closed maximal intervals of the continuous trace. Adjacent intervals
share a junction without asserting a derivative there. Open interiors express
the same classification under that convention. The two zero-speed intervals
are stops, not increasing or decreasing intervals. No trace is extended beyond
t=150 or before t=0.

## 1051

Use a != 0, x1+x2=-b/a and x1*x2=c/a, preserving the printed root columns.
The source decimals 0.7 and 1.3 are exact 7/10 and 13/10.

| Row | a | b | c | x1 | x2 | Actual Blank Cells |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | 2 | -13 | 6 | 1/2 | 6 | b, c |
| 2 | 3 | 48 | 180 | -10 | -6 | a, b |
| 3 | 50 | -100 | 91/2 | 7/10 | 13/10 | a, c |
| 4 | 1/3 | -5 | 12 | 12 | 3 | a, x1 |
| 5 | 6 | 1 | -10/3 | 2/3 | -5/6 | c, x2 |
| 6 | 9 | -2 | -7 | 1 | -7/9 | b, x2 |

1. b=-2(1/2+6)=-13; c=2(1/2)(6)=6.
2. a=180/[(-10)(-6)]=3; b=-3(-10-6)=48.
3. a=100/(0.7+1.3)=50; c=50(0.7)(1.3)=45.5=91/2.
4. The given root 3 gives 9a-15+12=0, so a=1/3.
   The root product gives x1=12/[(1/3)3]=12.
5. x2=-1/6-2/3=-5/6; c=6(2/3)(-5/6)=-10/3.
6. x2=-7/(9*1)=-7/9; b=-9(1-7/9)=-2.

Every completed a is nonzero. Each actual row fixes the otherwise possible
nonzero coefficient scaling. Each has one completion, no alternative branch
and no underdetermination. No zero denominator is used. There are no ambiguous
table cells held.

